{"title":"Carleman's Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Carleman's Inequality</b> states that for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nonnegative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nonnegative\">nonnegative</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Real numbers\">real numbers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c79701b36831dd0ffb63cd1498b0341b453a62b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_n\\}_{n\\ge 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"19\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/1/d111396ef9d06b06ad81fd4606ea2608b8ba13bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} (a_1 a_2 \\dotsm a_k)^{1/k} &lt; e \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} a_k ,\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"48\" />\nunless all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> are equal to zero.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carleman%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/e/42e3ce6946cc9d968f62759b1255cb3e97fa3101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_n = n \\left( 1 + \\frac{1}{n} \\right)^n = \\frac{(n+1)^n}{n^{n-1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"228\" height=\"44\" />.  Then for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/3403776f9ba18d681ba17e0ac7f18c0e7f96d3de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(c_1 \\dotsm c_k)^{1/k} = k+1.\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />\nThus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/e/f7e13ffcd2b1f6871eeb58fc32a73f63ee69b436.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty (a_1 \\dotsm a_k)^{1/k} = \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{(c_1a_1 \\dotsm c_ka_k)^{1/k}}{(c_1 \\dotsm c_k)^{1/k}} = \\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{(c_1a_1 \\dotsm c_ka_k)^{1/k}}{k+1} .\\]\" width=\"498\" height=\"48\" />\nNow, by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AM-GM\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"AM-GM\">AM-GM</a>,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d85af8e1bc46cb4b28aafc222347eb8ce6a156de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^\\infty \\frac{(c_1a_1 \\dotsm c_ka_k)^{1/k}}{k+1} \\le \\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{j=1}^k c_ja_j \\frac{1}{k(k+1)} = \\sum_{j=1}^\\infty \\sum_{k=j}^{\\infty} c_ja_j \\frac{1}{k(k+1)} .\\]\" width=\"530\" height=\"53\" />\nBut <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2540d5476572216b54834d61c7e73c1e4f0614.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{k(k+1)} = \\frac{1}{k} - \\frac{1}{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"173\" height=\"41\" />, so for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/9/e99b0f31a36d3e338b80329f973d10e964898f85.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=j}^\\infty \\frac{1}{k(k+1)} = \\sum_{k=j}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{k} - \\frac{1}{k+1} = \\lim_{N\\to \\infty} \\left( \\frac{1}{j} - \\frac{1}{N+1} \\right) = \\frac{1}{j} .\\]\" width=\"452\" height=\"50\" />\nTherefore\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e4939e2cf4dc1817802745b1b97de9f670d8f240.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{j=1}^{\\infty} \\sum_{k=j}^{\\infty} c_j a_j  \\frac{1}{k(k+1)} = \\sum_{j=1}^\\infty \\left( 1 + \\frac{1}{j} \\right)^j a_k .\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"52\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/142a5927d3af9e738055a0498ef646a6435f0ea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( 1 + \\frac{1}{j} \\right)^j&lt; e$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"110\" height=\"46\" /> for all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" />, the desired inequality holds.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carleman%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality\" title=\"Inequality\">Inequality</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nonnegative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nonnegative\">Nonnegative</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Carleman%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: References\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>Steele, J. M., <i>The Cauchy-Schwarz Master Class</i>, Cambridge University Press, ISBN 0-521-54677-X.</li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018075728\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 89/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3391/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6105:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018075728 and revision id 168854. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}